e3429cf21d14def\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"c11163ad5fceca70c9799038742c14bc1fc71962\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.022473520288864773, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/knn.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Replace insertion selection with original-order distance storage and three-way introselect on scratch distances, using a 4N partition-work guard before qsort fallback.\", \"Use up to four static contiguous OpenMP work units above 65,536 points, with a bitwise reduction detecting NaN distances.\", \"Build private strict/equal integer histograms, synchronize equal-count prefixes, and include only the earliest required cutoff ties.\", \"Resolve vote ties in native-char order; retain reference handling for NaNs, allocation failures and k<=1, and bypass distance generation when all points are selected.\", \"Free per-call temporary storage, including reference-path buffers.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"527a64a4c94e4bd5\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"3a7d23f015533c544eec39febb34ebc35c78779c\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.02722467357913653, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/knn.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Store retained neighbors in one contiguous array of distance, label, and input-ordinal records.\", \"Fill the array sequentially and build the heap bottom-up; subsequently reject against its root and update only a root-to-leaf path.\", \"Preserve reference selection semantics through ordinal tie-breaking, unused-label sentinels, and a serial fallback for unordered distances; release temporary storage on return.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"04956d5553ad4fa4\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"d3f1363694ab2367928e685e74589162c5ba3a9b\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.21674927820762, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/knn.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Track the occupied prefix of the contiguous distance and label buffers; reject noncompetitive points immediately once the buffers are full.\", \"Locate stable insertion positions with an upper-bound binary search and use memmove only on the occupied suffix.\", \"Switch permanently to the original insertion loops upon encountering a NaN distance, and free per-call scratch buffers after voting.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"ebf069bfdb1d42a8\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"7c2b4cfcdde656b98873019bd542322e419b1adc\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.7932351063936949, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/knn.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Replace the scalar insertion-position search with a four-lane NEON comparison scan that returns the earliest matching lane.\", \"Retain a scalar remainder loop and a compile-time scalar fallback when AArch64 NEON is unavailable.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"708557bb95c640df\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"78e3f8bf01756084671399003b65cb8a7a9368dd\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.8086952939629555, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/knn.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Maintain a per-call filled count capped at k and search only initialized distances.\", \"Remove sentinel equality checks from both NEON and scalar searches; return the prefix length when no comparison matches.\"]}}]}, \"target_as_data\": {\"architecture\": \"ARM64\", \"cpu_cores\": 4, \"gpus\": 0}, \"required_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"analysis\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"A\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"B\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"C\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"G\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"analysis\", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"G\"]}}",
